1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,483
Before you publish a page, you can see how it will look.

2
00:00:04,483 --> 00:00:08,864
Content Preview shows your changes in a separate tab while you type, and

3
00:00:08,864 --> 00:00:12,178
Preview Draft shows saved drafts before they go live.

4
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:14,200
In this video, we'll use both.

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:22,609
A content editor shows form fields, not the finished page.

6
00:00:22,609 --> 00:00:26,657
Content Preview renders the item as a page, so you can check a

7
00:00:26,657 --> 00:00:28,740
change before you publish it.

8
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:31,557
There are two ways to preview.

9
00:00:31,557 --> 00:00:36,382
Preview, in the editor, shows the values you are typing, even before you save.

10
00:00:36,382 --> 00:00:40,861
Preview Draft, in the content items list, shows the draft you saved, and

11
00:00:40,861 --> 00:00:43,790
it works without the Content Preview feature.

12
00:00:48,082 --> 00:00:50,913
Content Preview is a feature you enable.

13
00:00:50,913 --> 00:00:54,544
Open Tools, Features, and search for Content Preview.

14
00:00:54,544 --> 00:00:57,252
It is listed under Content Management.

15
00:00:57,752 --> 00:01:02,059
Select Enable, and a message confirms that the feature was enabled.

16
00:01:02,059 --> 00:01:05,482
Some setup recipes, such as Blog, enable it for you.

17
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,862
Select Edit on an article in Content, Content Items.

18
00:01:12,862 --> 00:01:16,630
The action bar at the bottom of the editor has a Preview button.

19
00:01:17,104 --> 00:01:18,252
Select Preview.

20
00:01:18,252 --> 00:01:21,972
A new tab opens and shows the article with the values that are

21
00:01:21,972 --> 00:01:24,324
in the form, without saving anything.

22
00:01:24,798 --> 00:01:28,455
Go back to the editor and change the Title and the Subtitle.

23
00:01:28,455 --> 00:01:32,333
A moment after you stop typing, the editor sends the form to the

24
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:35,048
site, and the preview tab shows the result.

25
00:01:35,503 --> 00:01:39,657
In the preview tab, the page shows the changed Title and Subtitle.

26
00:01:39,657 --> 00:01:43,523
The editor has to stay open for the preview to keep updating.

27
00:01:43,976 --> 00:01:46,718
Select Cancel to leave without saving.

28
00:01:46,718 --> 00:01:52,326
The content items list shows the original title, because live preview saves nothing.

29
00:01:52,788 --> 00:01:58,288
In the preview tab, a Preview Disconnected message appears, because you left the editor.

30
00:02:02,518 --> 00:02:06,587
An article with a saved draft shows a Draft badge beside Published in

31
00:02:06,587 --> 00:02:09,734
the content items list, with a Preview Draft button.

32
00:02:09,734 --> 00:02:12,338
Items without a draft have no such button.

33
00:02:12,819 --> 00:02:14,329
Select Preview Draft.

34
00:02:14,329 --> 00:02:18,466
A second tab opens with the saved draft of the article, displayed as

35
00:02:18,466 --> 00:02:19,919
a page of your site.

36
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,492
Back in the list, select View.

37
00:02:22,492 --> 00:02:27,492
It opens the published page, which shows the earlier Subtitle, because the draft

38
00:02:27,492 --> 00:02:29,760
is not live until you publish it.

39
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:37,303
Previewing needs the Preview content permission.

40
00:02:37,303 --> 00:02:43,557
Roles that can Edit content for others, or Publish or unpublish content for others, include it.

41
00:02:43,557 --> 00:02:47,210
Assign it to other roles under Access Control, Roles.

42
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:51,880
The editor and the preview tab have to stay in the same browser,

43
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,616
on the same site address.

44
00:02:53,616 --> 00:02:58,880
A preview link identifies temporary content that may be unpublished, so do not share it.

45
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:03,246
If the preview does not look like the page on your site, add

46
00:03:03,246 --> 00:03:05,602
the Preview part to the content type.

47
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:11,410
Edit the type under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, select Add Parts, and choose Preview.

48
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,430
The Preview part has a Pattern setting.

49
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:18,265
It holds an expression that returns the path of the page that displays

50
00:03:18,265 --> 00:03:22,050
the item, and the Preview button then loads that page from your site.

51
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:28,425
Preview checks your changes while you edit, and Preview Draft checks the version

52
00:03:28,425 --> 00:03:30,867
you saved, both before anything goes live.

53
00:03:30,867 --> 00:03:32,190
Thanks for watching.

